  P3:"Addition & complement rules", D1:"Random variables", D3:"Expected value & SD", D4:"Binomial structure",
  C4:"Normal table lookups", C5:"z-scores & tail values", C6:"Normal model in business",
  S1:"A statistic is a random variable", S2:"Sampling distribution of the mean", S3:"CLT and its conditions", S4:"Law of Large Numbers vs CLT",
  S5:"Sampling distribution of a proportion", S6:"Unbiasedness & sample size",
  E1:"Point vs interval estimator", E2:"CI for a mean (σ known / s)", E3:"When t, not z", E4:"CI for a proportion", E5:"Interpreting the confidence level", E6:"Sample size for a margin",
  H1:"Writing H0 and HA", H2:"Type I & Type II errors", H3:"p-values & failing to reject", H4:"One-sample z and t tests", H5:"Rejection region & conclusion", H6:"Power", H7:"Statistical vs practical significance",
  QC1:"Common vs assignable causes", QC2:"Control charts", QC3:"p chart: LCL set to 0", QC4:"Process capability", QC5:"Quality frameworks", QC6:"Control chart as repeated tests"
